                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 31 at 2:19PM HST until October 31 at 5:45PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "FFWHFO\n\nThe National Weather Service in Honolulu has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe island of Kauai in Kauai County\n\n* Until 545 PM HST.\n\n* At 219 PM HST, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain falling over the eastern slopes of Kauai with additional\nshowers moving in from the southwest. Rain was falling at a rate of\nup to 1 to 2 inches per hour. In addition to the Hanalei River, a\nrapid rise was also observed along the South Fork of the Wailua\nRiver. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly,\nespecially near the Hanalei Bridge on the Kuhio Highway and near\nthe mouth of the Wailua River. Kuhio Highway remains closed near\nthe Hanalei Bridge.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nThe entire island of Kauai.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nFlooding is occurring or is imminent. It is important to know where\nyou are relative to streams, rivers, or creeks which can become\nkillers in heavy rains. Campers and hikers should avoid streams or\ncreeks.",
                "response": "Avoid",
